    "subSection": "Item 61",
    "name": "Use validation not in accordance with regulations",
    "shortWording": "Use validation not in accordance with regulations",
    "part": "Part I",
    "setFine": 140.0,
    "totalPayable": 170.0,
    "summary": "Using permit validation proof in a way that breaks the regulations.",
    "elements": [
      {
        "id": "e1",
        "text": "The person used evidence of validation."
      },
      {
        "id": "e2",
        "text": "They used it in a way that did not follow the regulations."
      }
    ],
    "statutoryText": "12 (1) Every person who,\n(a) defaces or alters any number plate, evidence of validation or permit;\n(b) uses or permits the use of a defaced or altered number plate, evidence of validation or permit;\n(c) without the authority of the permit holder, removes a number plate from a motor vehicle or trailer; and\n(d) uses or permits the use of a number plate upon a vehicle other than a number plate authorized for use on that vehicle;\n(e) uses or permits the use of evidence of validation upon a number plate displayed on a motor vehicle other than evidence of validation furnished by the Ministry in respect of that motor vehicle; or\n(f) uses or permits the use of a number plate or evidence of validation other than in accordance with this Act and the regulations,\nis guilty of an offence and on conviction is liable to a fine of not less than $100 and not more than $1,000 or to imprisonment for not more than thirty days, or to both, and in addition the person's licence or permit may be suspended for not more than six months.",
    "procedureNotes": "HTA s. 12(1)(f); Sched. 43 Item 61. Part I set fine $140 + VFS $25 + $5.00 court cost = $170. Statutory range: $100–$1,000.",
