    "summary": "Driving a commercial motor vehicle on a public road with a device attached that shrinks the lens or dims the beam of a front lamp.",
    "elements": [
      {
        "id": "e1",
        "text": "The person drove a commercial motor vehicle (a truck, delivery vehicle, bus, ambulance, hearse, fire truck or hauling tractor)."
      },
      {
        "id": "e2",
        "text": "They drove on a highway (any public road, street, bridge or similar place the public drives on)."
      },
      {
        "id": "e3",
        "text": "One or both required front lamps were modified by an attached device that did ONE of these:",
        "options": [
          "a. Reduced the working area of the lenses",
          "b. Reduced the strength of the beam"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "statutoryText": "62 (7) No person shall drive upon a highway a motor vehicle if either or both of the lamps that are required on the front of the vehicle by subsections (1), (2) and (3),\n(a) are coated or covered with a coloured material; or\n(b) have been modified by the attachment to the lamps or the motor vehicle of any device that reduces the effective area of the lenses or the intensity of the beam of the lamps.",
    "procedureNotes": "HTA s. 62(7), s. 214(1); Sched. 43 Item 134.1. Part I set fine $200 + VFS $35 + $5.00 court cost = $240. Statutory range: $60–$1,000.",
