    "setFine": 85.0,
    "totalPayable": 110.0,
    "summary": "Operating a long or wide commercial vehicle or combination at night or in poor visibility without three top identification lamps at the front and rear.",
    "elements": [
      {
        "id": "e1",
        "text": "A commercial motor vehicle or combination with a trailer was longer than 9.2 metres or wider than 2.05 metres on a highway (any public road, street, bridge or similar place the public drives on)."
      },
      {
        "id": "e2",
        "text": "It was ONE of these times:",
        "options": [
          "a. From half an hour before sunset to half an hour after sunrise",
          "b. Any other time when poor light or bad weather kept people and vehicles from being clearly seen at 150 metres or less"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "e3",
        "text": "It failed to carry three evenly spaced green or amber front lamps (amber for a public vehicle) and three red rear lamps near the top, visible from 150 metres."
      }
    ],
    "statutoryText": "62 (11) When on a highway at any time from one-half hour before sunset to one-half hour after sunrise and at any other time when, due to insufficient light or unfavourable atmospheric conditions, persons and vehicles on the highway are not clearly discernible at a distance of 150 metres or less, every commercial motor vehicle or combination of a commercial motor vehicle and a trailer having a length in excess of 9.2 metres or a width in excess of 2.05 metres shall carry three lighted lamps displaying green or amber lights at the front, except in the case of a public vehicle which shall display amber lights at the front, and three lighted lamps displaying red lights at the rear, and the lights of each colour shall be evenly placed not less than 150 millimetres nor more than 310 millimetres apart along a horizontal line as near the top of the commercial motor vehicle or combination of a commercial motor vehicle and a trailer as the permanent structure permits, and shall be visible for distances of 150 metres from the front and rear respectively of the commercial motor vehicle or combination of a commercial motor vehicle and a trailer.",
    "procedureNotes": "HTA s. 62(11), s. 214(1); Sched. 43 Item 137. Part I set fine $85 + VFS $20 + $5.00 court cost = $110. Statutory range: $60–$1,000.",
