    "id": "HTA:item-144",
    "statute": "HTA",
    "category": "equipment",
    "section": "62(19)",
    "subSection": "Item 144",
    "name": "Improper number plate light",
    "shortWording": "Improper number plate light",
    "part": "Part I",
    "setFine": 85.0,
    "totalPayable": 110.0,
    "summary": "Failing to have a white rear lamp of at least three candela lighting up the rear number plate at night or in poor visibility.",
    "elements": [
      {
        "id": "e1",
        "text": "There was a rear lamp on a motor vehicle or trailer."
      },
      {
        "id": "e2",
        "text": "It was ONE of these times:",
        "options": [
          "a. From half an hour before sunset to half an hour after sunrise",
          "b. Any other time when poor light or bad weather kept people and vehicles from being clearly seen at 150 metres or less"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "e3",
        "text": "The lamp failed ONE of these:",
        "options": [
          "a. Was less than three candela",
          "b. Did not light up the numbers on the number plate",
          "c. Was not placed in the spot provided for the plate",
          "d. Did not face rear and shine a white light only on the plate"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "statutoryText": "62 (19) The lamp on the rear of a motor vehicle or trailer shall be of at least three candela and shall be so placed that it will, at any time from one-half hour before sunset to one-half hour after sunrise and at any other time when, due to insufficient light or unfavourable atmospheric conditions, persons and vehicles on the highway are not clearly discernible at a distance of 150 metres or less, illuminate the numbers on the number plate, or, if provision is made on the number plate or on any attachment furnished or required by the Ministry for affixing the lamp, it shall be affixed in the position or space provided, and the lamp shall face to the rear and reflect on the number plate a white light only.",
    "procedureNotes": "HTA s. 62(19), s. 214(1); Sched. 43 Item 144. Part I set fine $85 + VFS $20 + $5.00 court cost = $110. Statutory range: $60–$1,000.",
