    "name": "Overweight vehicle kg. Class A Highway",
    "shortWording": "Overweight vehicle … kg. Class A Highway",
    "part": "Part I",
    "setFine": null,
    "totalPayable": "Schedule A Weight Scale (min $100)",
    "summary": "Driving on a Class A highway with a gross vehicle weight over the legal maximum.",
    "elements": [
      {
        "id": "e1",
        "text": "The person drove a vehicle on a Class A highway (any public road, street, bridge or similar place the public drives on)."
      },
      {
        "id": "e2",
        "text": "The gross vehicle weight exceeded the legal maximum."
      }
    ],
    "statutoryText": "118 (1) Subject to section 110, no vehicle or combination of vehicles shall be operated on a Class A Highway where the gross vehicle weight exceeds,(a) the axle unit weight on the front axle, not exceeding the maximum weight permitted on the axle under section 116, plus the sum of the maximum allowable weights for all other axle units of the vehicle or combination of vehicles as set out in section 116;(b) the axle unit weight on the front axle, not exceeding the maximum weight permitted on the axle under section 116, plus the sum of the maximum allowable weights for any two axle groups, three axle groups or four axle groups, or any combination thereof, as set out in section 117, plus the maximum allowable weight for any axle unit or units excluding the front axle and excluding any axle unit or units which are part of an axle group, as set out in section 116; or(c) that weight prescribed in the regulations.(2) Where subsection (1) refers to a weight under or set out in section 116 or 117, the reference includes a weight specified by regulation under subsection 116 (1.1) or 117 (2).",
    "procedureNotes": "HTA s. 118, s. 125(1); Sched. 43 Item 330. Overweight Schedule A scale per 100 kg (or fraction): <2,500 kg ($5/100kg), 2,500–4,999 ($6), 5,000–7,499 ($8), 7,500–9,999 ($12), min $100.00 + VFS + $5 cost. Overload ≥ 10,000 kg requires Part III. Statutory range: $100–$1,000.",
