    "subSection": "Item 479",
    "name": "Pass street car improperly",
    "shortWording": "Pass street car improperly",
    "part": "Part I",
    "setFine": 85.0,
    "totalPayable": 110.0,
    "summary": "Passing a street car stopped to pick up or drop off passengers where there is no safety zone.",
    "elements": [
      {
        "id": "e1",
        "text": "The driver approached a street car stopped to pick up or drop off passengers."
      },
      {
        "id": "e2",
        "text": "The person passed the street car before passengers got on or safely reached the side of the street."
      }
    ],
    "statutoryText": "166 (1) Where a person in charge of a vehicle or on horseback or leading a horse on a highway overtakes a street car or a car of an electric railway, operated in or near the centre of the roadway, which is stationary for the purpose of taking on or discharging passengers, he or she shall not pass the car or approach nearer than 2 metres measured back from the nearest door of the car that the person is approaching and through which passengers may get on or off until the passengers have got on or got safely to the side of the street, as the case may be, but this subsection does not apply where a safety zone has been set aside and designated by a by-law passed under section 9, 10 or 11 of the Municipal Act, 2001 or under section 7 or 8 of the City of Toronto Act, 2006.",
    "procedureNotes": "HTA s. 166(1), s. 214(1); Sched. 43 Item 479. Part I set fine $85 + VFS $20 + $5.00 court cost = $110. Statutory range: $60–$1,000.",
